"""Files to hand to an upload field.

Generated by AutoQA.

A browser never tells a page where a chosen file really lives - that is a
security rule, not an oversight - so a recording can only capture the name you
picked:

    upload  photos_input   files: ["IMG_1234.jpg"]

Replayed as `set_input_files("IMG_1234.jpg")` that looks for a file sitting next
to the test. It is not there; it is on the machine where the recording was made.
Playwright raises, the form never submits, and every step after it fails - on a
form with nothing wrong with it.

Playwright will also take a file from memory: a name, a type and the bytes. One
is built here instead, so there is nothing to place anywhere and the suite runs
on any machine that checks it out.

The image is a placeholder and says so on its face. A test can prove the listing
was created; it cannot prove your photograph came back, because your photograph
was never in the recording.
"""

